{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0291","billNumberShort":"H.B. 291","billNumberLong":"HB0291","fileNumber":"2026FL0653","shortTitle":"Security and Land Restriction Amendments","currentSubVersion":"0","currentMinVersion":"3","primeSponsor":"PIERUC","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Pierucci, Candice B.","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"MCKELMK","floorSponsorName":"Sen. McKell, Michael K.","floorSponsorHouse":"S","generalProvisions":"This bill amends provisions dealing with the sale of land to restricted foreign entities.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>lowers the percentage of ownership a restricted foreign entity may maintain in a separate entity before the separate entity is considered a restricted foreign entity;<hr><ltbullet>provides that the Department of Public Safety (department) shall send a letter to an entity the department suspects of being a restricted foreign entity;<hr><ltbullet>provides that an entity to which the department sends a letter shall provide evidence that demonstrates the entity is not a restricted foreign entity within 30 days after the day on which the entity receives the letter;<hr><ltbullet>provides that the attorney general shall coordinate with the Division of Facilities and Construction Management when conducting a sale of a restricted foreign entity's interest in land;<hr><ltbullet>provides that if an entity does not respond to a letter from the department, the department may impose a fine for each day the entity does not respond; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Austin Weenig","fiscalAnalyst":"Steven M. Allred","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/24/2026","trackingID":"OKXBULDNPB","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-20 14:23:43.070","actionC